<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Performance across Datasets</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we provide the complete per-model, per-dataset results that complement the aggregated deltas shown in Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5.3 Results on Other Datasets ‣ 5 Results ‣ Mind the Gap:␣A Closer Look at Tokenization forMultiple-Choice Question Answering with LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> of the main paper. We observe a consistent trend in favor of tokenizing the space together with the answer letter across datasets and model families. Even our largest evaluated model, Qwen 2.5 72B, shows a substantial gap of 11.7 accuracy points (on HellaSwag), indicating that larger models are also susceptible to such tokenization effects.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T8" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
